A||||8||Hartz||Need advice - V8's and clutches||||11||
Z||000000||Hartz||03-12-2001||10:17 AM||||I went and looked at a V8 conversion this past weekend.  I loved the car, but the force required to use the clutch was unbelieveably heavy.  It's the heaviest clutch I've ever driven!  I drive a Firehawk on a daily basis, so I'm not looking for a Honda Accord clutch or anything, but I mean this thing was straight out of NASCAR or something.<P>If I am going to seriously consider this car, I'd have to have the clutch changed.  I already have one Fiero my wife won't drive - I don't need a second.  Just getting used to it is probably not an option.  If it were just me, then maybe, but not in this case.<P>I did some searching for clutch info, and have seen mixed reviews.  For those of you with V8's (or big torque 3800's, or others?) - what clutch are you using, and how does it hold up?  Any slipping?  How's the pedal effort?  What's your recommendation?  Any advice, stories, thoughts, or opinions?<P>Any help appreciated.<P>Thanks,<BR>Hartz<P>'85 SE V6 Turbo<P>hartzfeld@mindspring.com||||reg||11
Z||000001||Formula88||03-12-2001||11:19 AM||||Also along this line, can anyone give us some info on the clutch/tranny longevity behind an engine swap.  Please, no anectodal evidence.  Just let us know if you have any 1st hand experience.  I know the whole line that you can break any tranny if you abuse it. True, but why put a 400hp engine in your Fiero if you have to baby it all the time?  If you can't DRIVE the car, what's the point?  And I'm not talking about dumping the clutch a 5000rpm and powershifting every gear at every stoplight.  But the car should be able to be driven enthusiastically, with daily bursts of full throttle.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Alex4mula||03-12-2001||12:12 PM||||Yeah, I would also like to know. I'm interested in getting a fastback Fiero for a V8 conversion. I would like an automatic setup with it. <BR>Can a V8, lets say with 300HP-350HP, with a stock Fiero Auto tranny be floored from a stop without braking the tranny? If I'm at speed and I floor it and the tranny down shift, will it break? I mean, just doing what you do with any auto tranny. I'm not talking about putting slicks and having power brake launches. Just normal fun. Would love to hear from Archie. I think he's the most experienced in this topic.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Hartz||03-12-2001||12:48 PM||||OK - I did not intend for this to become some V8 holy war here, and I can see that this is where it's going.  Perhaps it is best if people e-mail me their thoughts.  For those of you with high output engines, and V8s in particular, I need:<P>What clutch are you using?<BR>Does it work? (no slipping, problems, etc.)<BR>How's the pedal feel?<P>Sorry to have caused a stir.<P>Hartz<BR>'85 SE V6 Turbo<P>hartzfeld@mindspring.com||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FST2M6||03-12-2001||01:10 PM||||I've driven Bbbad Gts V8 and it was easier to drive than my V6. he has a Centerforce Df. I had one but it died. if your putting down 300hp in anything your gunna split the case on the tranny if ya RAIL on it all the time... Jeffs V8 lays down 207hp-260lbft and it'll $hit git! it pulls like a train till you let off the gas. chirps 3rd and keeps running... <P><BR>-----<BR>oh andd as for the Automatic question.. uum Shaun41178 is running nitrous.. and once agian. if it'll handelt eh shock loads of nitrous i'm SURE it'll be happy with the more gradual loads of a V*.. even on a down shift... <P>archie builds the piss out of his cars and has for ever and i've never heard of one failing for any enthusiastic driving... for drag racing yeah. but not everyday .. backroads playing.. or the occasional Play at a stop light.<BR>me laying down 309.7lbft under nitrous didn't kill the 4spd i had.. and 253lbft (normal street shot) didn't kill my tranny and I had a solid unsprund disc. and Nitrous is WAY more sudden then any V8.. placing CRAZY explosive loads on all the driveline parts... thats why my Centerforce choked. I'm sure me beating the crap out of the car would have done somthing.. but.. no leaks, no whines.. no bad synchros.. just nice solid shifting and lots of Street light stomping. I'm sure with the constant and consistant V8 hp and Tq you'll be much safer with the higher number than a V6 and nitrous.<p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 03-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||BBBAD GT||03-12-2001||01:24 PM||||Actually, the DF in my V8 has a lighter pedel effort than my sold 87 GT (with stock clutch).  It holds it at full throttle, but when Chris had a 'hot' V8 (400+ HP), the clutch would slip at high rpms.  Centerforce can upgrade your std DF clutch for like 1-200 bux.  No complaints.<P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero/V8sig.jpg">      <P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD V8</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT (sold)</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Alex4mula||03-12-2001||01:26 PM||||Thanks 1FST. I guess I'll be safe if I find a good deal on an auto fastback.<P> I don't see where is the war here. We just took an opportunity for info. Anyway Hartz info request should take priority. Sorry if we misled your thread..||||reg||1
Z||000007||Hartz||03-12-2001||03:00 PM||||Nah, I guess holy war is a strong term, but I've seen threads in the past of folks debating a wide world of V8 issues, and I didn't want to go down that road.  <P>90% of the info I've got says Centerforce DF clutch is the way to go, but the guy who owns the car now was skeptical, because he knew someone who used "a Centerforce clutch" (don't know which one, trying to track that down) and the clutch would slip at "anything over 4000 rpm" or even "going up a simple hill."  All circumstancial, but hey - I don't want to buy the car, pay big $$$ for a new clutch, and then either have the car be undriveable, or have the pedal feel be as bad or worse than it is now.<P>Thanks all,<BR>Hartz||||reg||12
Z||000008||Alex4mula||03-12-2001||03:09 PM||||Check with Fieroshop (George) in CA. I think he has a product for V8s. I have a kevlar clutch from him for my 3.4 and I'm very satisfied with it. Low effort and great grip. Give him a call.||||reg||1
